{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgH9iGKxrMmkNGyxZ2B3u","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Top 5 intermediaries in Fund IV deal flow\n\n| Rank | Intermediary | Betweenness | Thesis deals (5 yrs) | Our touchpoints (24 mo) | Coverage gap |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Cedar Row Partners | 7,507.4 | 14 | 14 | No |\n| 2 | Harbor Lane Advisors | 1,667.4 | 9 | 1 | **Yes** |\n| 3 | Wilby Securities | 1,113.1 | 4 | 5 | No |\n| 4 | Umberby & Co. | 1,061.2 | 4 | 7 | No |\n| 5 | Wexhall Bank Capital | 777.3 | 3 | 4 | No |\n\nThe ranking uses betweenness: how often an intermediary sits on the shortest deal-flow route between two firms. The ranking covers 34 intermediaries.\n\n- **Cedar Row Partners:** the main hub, with about 4.5× the betweenness of #2. It advised 14 deals in our sectors, and we have been in touch 14 times, so coverage matches its importance.\n- **Harbor Lane Advisors:** the #2 bridge, with 9 deals in our sectors, but only 1 touchpoint with us in 24 months. It is the one coverage gap: a top-4 bridge with contact at or below the bottom quartile.\n- **Wilby Securities:** #3 bridge, 4 deals in our sectors, 5 touchpoints.\n- **Umberby & Co.:** #4 bridge, 4 deals in our sectors, 7 touchpoints.\n- **Wexhall Bank Capital:** #5 bridge, 3 deals in our sectors, 4 touchpoints.\n\nA CRM screen would show Harbor Lane Advisors as a minor contact with one touchpoint. It can't see that Harbor Lane is the second most important bridge in our sectors' deal flow."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":975,"cache_read_input_tokens":32911,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":975,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"sessi